course: dictionary
lesson: 7235
title: Tiny drifting plants of the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look hard, but the words around them give clues. «Tiny drifting algae and bacteria called phytoplankton are the producers of the ocean.» Tiny and drifting tell you they are very small and float with the water. Producers are things that make food, so phytoplankton must make food too.
explain: «Tiny drifting plants called phytoplankton bloom in the Southern Ocean in spring.» The sentence calls them plants, so phytoplankton is a kind of plant. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Tiny drifting plants bloom in spring" still makes sense, so the guess fits.
explain: Context also helps with bloom. Here it does not mean a flower. A bloom is a sudden burst of growth, so huge numbers of these tiny plants grow at once and turn the water green. Satellites in space can see these green blooms.
fact: Phytoplankton are tiny living things, mostly too small to see.
fact: They float near the surface of seas and lakes.
fact: Like plants, they make their own food using sunlight.
fact: Phytoplankton are producers: zooplankton eat them, fish eat zooplankton, and bigger animals such as whales eat fish.
fact: They make roughly half of the oxygen on Earth, so we all need them to breathe.
exercise: «Tiny drifting plants called phytoplankton bloom in the Southern Ocean in spring.» What are phytoplankton, according to this sentence? | Birds that fly over the sea | Large fish that swim in groups | Rocks on the seabed | *Tiny drifting plants
exercise: Phytoplankton use sunlight to do something, just like plants on land. What do they make? | Sand for the beaches | Clouds for the rain | Whale songs | *Their own food
exercise: «Tiny drifting plants called phytoplankton bloom in the Southern Ocean in spring.» What does bloom mean here? | A storm at sea | A kind of whale | *A sudden burst of growth, turning the water green | A flower in a garden
test: Why are phytoplankton called producers? | They produce loud noises under the sea | They are the biggest animals in the sea | *They make their own food, and other creatures eat them | They live only in lakes
test: «Whale poo helps feed them because it contains iron they need.» What does this tell us about phytoplankton? | They live on land | They eat whales | They never need food | *They need iron to grow
exam: Which food chain is in the right order? | Whale, fish, zooplankton, phytoplankton | *Phytoplankton, zooplankton, fish, whale | Zooplankton, whale, fish, phytoplankton | Fish, whale, phytoplankton, zooplankton
